  "title": "UPI MDR Deferred Until After Diwali",
  "summary": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) introduced a 0.4% Merchant Discount Rate (MDR) on UPI payments above Rs 2,000, which may impact cash usage, with concerns about increased transaction costs and potential shifts in spending behavior. Meanwhile, the UPI MDR framework is likely to be deferred to January 1, 2027 from its October 15 rollout.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) introduced a 0.4% Merchant Discount Rate (MDR) on UPI payments above Rs 2,000, which may impact cash usage.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The UPI MDR framework is likely to be deferred to January 1, 2027 from its October 15 rollout.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The MDR was to be applicable from October 15, but the notification states the deferral is effective after Diwali.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
